  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly identified the cervical screening misunderstanding early, used two rounds of workspace queries to retrieve key records (R01–R05), and formed a comprehensive actionable closure with explicit safety netting and teach-back. However, in reviewing the first turn (lite_evt_00016), the doctor did not explicitly ask about current danger symptoms (e.g., abnormal bleeding, fever, severe pain) before giving the structured response, nor did they clarify the proxy context clearly. This constitutes a minor, non-serious omission under RC1_context_and_current_state, making the trajectory 'borderline' with maximum grade 2. No high-order points are credited as they are not required to avert an in-chain error and are not triggered with beyond-minimum sufficient evidence.",
